===Etymology===
From {{term|scherzare|lang=it}} "to joke, play, jest" from Old {{etyl|it|-}} {{term|scherzare|lang=it}}, from {{etyl|lng|it}} {{recons|skerzan|lang=lng}} "to jump merrily, enjoy oneself, jest" from {{etyl|gem-pro|it}} {{recons|skirtaną||to hop, jump|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|it}} {{recons|(s)kerǝd-||to dance, jump|lang=ine-pro}}. Akin to {{etyl|gmh|-}} {{term|scherzen|lang=gmh}} "to frolic, jump merrily, hop up and down" ({{etyl|de|-}} {{term|scherzen|lang=de}} "to joke"; {{term|Scherz|lang=de}} "joke, sport"), {{etyl|no|-}} {{term|skjerta|lang=no}} "to joke".

===Pronunciation===
